  "lineage": "Oklahoma country grew out of the Tulsa and Oklahoma City ballroom and radio circuit of the 1930s–60s, codified by Bob Wills' Texas Playboys at Cain's Ballroom, Hank Thompson's Brazos Valley Boys and Wanda Jackson — 130–180 BPM western-swing two-beats and polkas with amplified steel guitar, fiddle section, jazz-derived horn or piano comping and Charlie Christian-lineage electric lead, plus the laid-back Tulsa Sound shuffle of Leon Russell and J.J. Cale that later loosened the tempo and softened the vocal to a mumble.",
